# REAL FINDING (adjacent to the withdrawn false positive).
# The shape-catalog container's own dc:description still narrates the retired D77 design.

<urn:uuid:1d475db3-a75c-4700-9891-83a6316fc21a>
    a as:Announce, mem:RealignAction, prov:Activity ;
    as:actor <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    as:target </vault/wiki/working/curator-proposals/> ;
    as:object </vault/meta/shapes/.meta> ;                  # the stale description lives here
    prov:wasAssociatedWith <urn:agent:claude-code> ;
    prov:used </vault/.claude/skills/decision-lookup#D98> ;  # intended truth (decision)
    prov:used <https://pod.vardeman.me/vault/meta/shapes/> ; # operational truth (live listing: 18 files)
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <urn:prior:catalog-description-D77> ;
    mem:stalenessClass mem:ProseDrift ;
    mem:rationale "The container dc:description reads 'wiki-memory L3 SHACL shapes (D77). Five shapes: page, source, person, procedure, working.' This is three supersessions stale: D77's five-shape catalog was retired by D98 (8 NodeShapes / 11 files); the live container now holds 18 shape files (the 11 D98 files + AddressBook overlay shapes contact-card/organization-card/membership/group per D87/D88 + owner-identity overlay shapes webid-profile/pod-owner-preferences per D89/D90 + the re-introduced source.shacl.ttl class-extension example, 2026-05-23). The named files 'source/procedure' no longer match (procedure->howto, source is now an extension example not a core shape). Repair direction: prose -> reality. The corrected description should cite D98 as the current catalog decision and not pin a hard shape count in prose (counts drift; let the listing be the source of truth)." ;
    as:published "2026-05-23T22:33:36Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

